Z||000000||86SE||08-09-2000||01:57 AM||||I decoded all my RPO numbers and came across a few that I thought were interesting.  It says I have 'Heavy Duty Special Suspension' and it says I have 'Special Rally Suspension'.  Did all '86 Fieros have these options?  I really dont feel anything special about my suspension......<P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Yellow Fiero||||reg||5
Z||000001||Monkeyman||08-09-2000||02:08 AM||||Just various upgrades to the stock suspension, I would assume.  I wouldn't worry too much about it now unless you're planning a 100% original restoration.  You're suspension has either been replaced or needs to be.  There's no way that 15 year old shocks, struts, etc are any good.||||reg||1
Z||000002||nivlek68||08-09-2000||12:31 PM||||86se i also have the 86sc special(whatever that means)it has the rpo coeds F41 &lt;suspension,heavy duty,front and rear(special)&gt;  Y99  &lt;special rally suspension package&gt; then 6hz,7hz,8xd,9xd they are the codes for springs. the only thing i know for sure is she handles great and the previous owner had replaced the shocks,struts.i had to have the four wheel algniment. good luck with your 1st fiero,the 86sc is mine 1st too.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000003||theogre||08-09-2000||12:59 PM||||The only way you'd notice is to drive a Fiero w/o the options. You'd notice real quick.<P>those options include:<BR>heavier springs<BR>I bevlieve heavier front sway bar<BR>3 turn steering instead of 3.5(lock to lock at the steering wheel)<BR>May also have had better shocks and struts but like said above those are no longer relavant for most cars.||||reg||1
